BUILDING UPLINKOS GOLD ON LINUX
===============================

The supported build uses Allegro 5, TinyXML2, SDL 1.2/SDL_mixer, OpenGL,
FreeType, and the bundled legacy libraries. Run commands from the repository
root.

Ubuntu 24.04 dependencies
-------------------------

  sudo apt-get update
  sudo apt-get install -y \
    build-essential pkg-config autoconf automake libtool \
    ca-certificates curl desktop-file-utils file patchelf \
    libx11-dev libxext-dev libgl1-mesa-dev libglu1-mesa-dev \
    libsdl1.2-dev libsdl-mixer1.2-dev \
    libfreetype-dev libtiff-dev libjpeg-dev zlib1g-dev \
    liballegro5-dev liballegro-image5-dev liballegro-ttf5-dev \
    libtinyxml2-dev

Build
-----

  make -C contrib/FTGL-2.1.2 -j4
  make -C contrib/tcp4u.331/src -f ../Unix/Makefile -j4
  make -C contrib/irclib -j4
  make -C contrib/unrar -j4
  make -C lib -j4
  make -C uplink/src -f Makefile.linux -j4

`Makefile.linux` defines `USE_ALLEGRO5`; without that define the HD manager is
compiled out and only the legacy Eclipse interface appears.

Deploy and run
--------------

  install -m 755 uplink/src/uplink.full uplink/bin/uplink
  cd uplink/bin
  ./uplink

Running from `uplink/bin` is required. The program loads `data.dat`, the other
archive files, and `uplinkHD/` relative to the executable path.

AppImage
--------

After building `uplink.full`, create the self-contained x86_64 AppImage with:

  packaging/appimage/build-appimage.sh uplink/src/uplink.full dist

The script downloads the official linuxdeploy x86_64 AppImage and verifies its
pinned SHA-256 before execution. The output is
`dist/UplinkOS-GOLD-v1.04-x86_64.AppImage` plus its checksum.

The AppImage contains all ten runtime data archives, the unpacked `data/` and
`music/` directories, and the complete `uplinkHD/` tree as regular files.
Nothing in the package points back into the source checkout. If FUSE is
unavailable, launch it with `APPIMAGE_EXTRACT_AND_RUN=1`.

User data
---------

Linux profiles are written beneath `$HOME/.uplink/`:

- `<agent>.usr` and `<agent>.tmp`: encrypted SAV67 profile and recovery copy
- `<agent>_notes.xml`: UplinkOS notes
- `<agent>_hotkeys.xml`: user hotkey overrides when changed
- `options`: encrypted options

A headless smoke run can use Xvfb. Missing ALSA hardware only disables audio; it
does not prevent graphics or profile verification.

Build products
--------------

Objects, static archives, `uplink/src/uplink.full`, and the deployed
`uplink/bin/uplink` are ignored build outputs. Do not commit them.
